  "snapshot": {
    "id": "tpch-lake-proposal-streaming-001",
    "source_revision": null,
    "coverage": "complete",
    "scope_description": "Proposal over tpch-lake revision 2: what if PartsHub orders streamed into Snowflake instead of loading nightly? Snowpipe Streaming fills a new ORDERS_LIVE table and the marts become dynamic tables with a 1-minute lag. Unchanged parts keep their IDs and basis. New and changed parts are declared and start with \"Proposed:\". The nightly load stays in the model, marked \"Proposed: removed\", so a walkthrough can label it.",
    "omissions": [
      "Sample schemas other than TPCH_SF1 (TPCDS, larger TPC-H scales) are not used.",
      "Warehouse sizing, roles and grants are outside this model.",
      "PartsHub is illustrative: TPC-H describes the business but ships no application code, so its apps, orders database and nightly load are declared, not cited.",
      "Rehearsed in the zero-copy clone FILAGREE_WHATIF: only the revenue dynamic table, built over the unchanging sample share. Snowpipe Streaming, ORDERS_LIVE and the supplier scorecard dynamic table were not tried.",
      "Cost is not modelled: a FULL refresh every minute re-reads 6M lines. Incremental refresh needs change tracking on every source, which the share does not allow."
    ]
  },
